GitHub repository and owner IDs are sometimes represented as integers in various APIs and payloads, even though they are strings in OIDC claims. To prevent silent parsing failures if a tool encodes them as integers, consider stringifying them robustly if they are not null.

```dart
      final id = github['repository_id'];
      if (id != null) {
        final idStr = '$id'.trim();
        if (idStr.isNotEmpty) repositoryId = idStr;
      }
      final ownerId = github['repository_owner_id'];
      if (ownerId != null) {
        final ownerIdStr = '$ownerId'.trim();
        if (ownerIdStr.isNotEmpty) repositoryOwnerId = ownerIdStr;
